===Noun===
[[Image:Batong, Nordisk familjebok.png|right|thumb|A law enforcement baton]]
{{en-noun}}

# {{sid|en|Q392326}}{{lb|en|countable}} A [[heavy]] object, often a kind of [[stick]], intended for use as a [[bludgeon]]ing [[weapon]] or a [[plaything]].
#* {{RQ:Maxwell Mirror and the Lamp|chapter=12|passage=There were many wooden chairs for the bulk of his visitors, and two wicker armchairs with red cloth cushions for superior people. From the packing-cases had emerged some Indian '''clubs''',{{nb...}}, and all these articles{{nb...}} made a scattered and untidy decoration that Mrs. Clough assiduously dusted and greatly cherished.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|author=Drachinifel|title=Guadalcanal Campaign - The Big Night Battle: Night 1 (IJN 3(?) : 2 USN)|date=10 March 2021|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Em_PuLURII4|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20221017005233/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Em_PuLURII4|archivedate=17 October 2022|accessdate=6 November 2022|time=5:50|text=The attack also afforded ''Helena'' to a front-seat view of ''literal air-to-air melee combat'', as one Wildcat pilot of the Cactus Air Force, who was swooping in to help break up the attack, found himself out of machine-gun ammo; instead, he dropped his landing gear, positioned himself above the nearest bomber, and begun ''beating'' it to death, in midair, using his landing gear as '''clubs'''.  After a bit of evasive action that the fighter easily kept up with, the repeated slamming broke something important, and the bomber spiralled down into the sea.}}
## {{sid|en|Q1054671}}{{lb|en|countable|golf}} An implement to hit the ball in certain ball games, such as [[golf]].
## {{lb|en|countable|rhythmic gymnastics}} An item used during [[routine]]s, the [[apparatus]] consisting of a set of two clubs.
# {{sid|en|Q988108}}{{lb|en|countable}} An [[association]] of [[member]]s joining together for some common purpose, especially [[sports]] or [[recreation]].
#* {{RQ:Besant Ivory Gate|III
|passage=At half-past nine on this Saturday evening, the parlour of the Salutation Inn, High Holborn, contained most of its customary visitors.{{...}}In former days every tavern of repute kept such a room for its own select circle, a '''club''', or society, of habitués, who met every evening, for a pipe and a cheerful glass.}}
## {{lb|en|specifically|US| Canada}} a primarily student-managed group of members joining together for some common purpose or interest, affiliated with a university
##: {{cot|en|society|q1=UK}}
## {{lb|en|archaic}} The fees associated with belonging to such a club.
##* '''1783''', {{w|Benjamin Franklin}}:<sup>[http://press-pubs.uchicago.edu/founders/documents/v1ch16s12.html ]</sup>
##*: He can have no right to the benefits of Society, who will not pay his '''Club''' towards the Support of it.
# A joint charge of expense, or any person's share of it; a contribution to a common fund.
#* {{RQ:L'Estrange Fables of Aesop|passage=They laid down the '''Club'''.}}
#* '''17 Mat 1660''', {{w|Samuel Pepys}}, ''diary''
#*: first we went and dined at a French house , but paid 10[[shilling|s]] for our part of the '''club'''
# {{senseid|en|establishment}} An establishment that provides [[stage]]d [[entertainment]], often with food and drink, such as a [[nightclub]].
#: {{ux|en|She was sitting in a jazz '''club''', sipping wine and listening to a bass player's solo.}}
# {{lb|en|card games}} A black [[clover]] shape (&clubs;), one of the four symbols used to mark the [[suit]]s of [[playing card]]s.
## A playing card marked with such a symbol.
##: {{ux|en|I've got only one '''club''' in my hand.}}
# {{lb|en|humorous}} Any set of people with a shared characteristic.
#: {{ux|en|You also hate ''Night Court''?&nbsp; [[join the club|Join the '''club''']].}}
#: {{ux|en|Michael stood you up?&nbsp; Welcome to the '''club'''.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|work=Smithsonian Magazine|author=Tony Perrottet|title=A Deep Dive Into the Plans to Take Tourists to the ‘Titanic’|year=2019|text=He also wanted to be only the second person to travel solo to at least that depth, the other being James Cameron, who in 2012 took an Australian-built sub into the Mariana Trench, reaching Challenger Deep, the ocean’s deepest point, touching down at close to 36,000 feet. “That’s a nice '''club''' to be a part of,” Rush says. Two weeks later, that '''club''' welcomed a new member, when a Texas businessman named Victor Vescovo reached 27,000 feet in his own experimental submersible.}}
# A [[club sandwich]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|author=Joanne M. Anderson|title=Small-town Restaurants in Virginia|page=123
|passage=Crab cake sandwiches, tuna melts, chicken '''clubs''', salmon cakes, and prime-rib sandwiches are usually on the menu.}}
# The slice of bread in the middle of a [[club sandwich]].
# {{lb|en|{{w|World War I}}–{{w|World War II}}|_|military slang}} The [[propeller]] of an [[aeroplane]].<ref name="Lighter">{{R:en:Lighter:1972|page=34}}</ref>
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} A [[set]] which is both [[closed]] and [[unbounded]].

